{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":18,"code":"JOB","name":"Job","testament":"OT"},"chapter":13,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"JOB 13:1"},"Lo, mine eye hath seen all ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["this,"]}," mine ear hath heard and understood it. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"JOB 13:2"},"What ye know, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["the same"]}," do I know also: I ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["am"]}," not inferior unto you. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"JOB 13:3"},"Surely I would speak to the Almighty, and I desire to reason with God. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"JOB 13:4"},"But ye ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," forgers of lies, ye ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," all physicians of no value. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"JOB 13:5"},"Oh that ye would altogether hold your peace! and it should be your wisdom. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"JOB 13:6"},"Hear now my reasoning, and hearken to the pleadings of my lips. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"JOB 13:7"},"Will ye speak wickedly for God? and talk deceitfully for him? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:7"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"JOB 13:8"},"Will ye accept his person? will ye contend for God? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"JOB 13:9"},"Is it good that he should search you out? or as one man mocketh another, do ye ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["so"]}," mock him? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"JOB 13:10"},"He will surely reprove you, if ye do secretly accept persons. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"JOB 13:11"},"Shall not his excellency make you afraid? and his dread fall upon you? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"JOB 13:12"},"Your remembrances ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," like unto ashes, your bodies to bodies of clay. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"JOB 13:13"},"Hold your peace, let me alone, that I may speak, and let come on me what ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["will. "]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"JOB 13:14"},"Wherefore do I take my flesh in my teeth, and put my life in mine hand? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"JOB 13:15"},"Though he slay me, yet will I trust in him: but I will maintain mine own ways before him. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:15"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"JOB 13:16"},"He also ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["shall be"]}," my salvation: for an hypocrite shall not come before him. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:16"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"JOB 13:17"},"Hear diligently my speech, and my declaration with your ears. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:17"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"18","sid":"JOB 13:18"},"Behold now, I have ordered ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["my"]}," cause; I know that I shall be justified. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:18"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"19","sid":"JOB 13:19"},"Who ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," he ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that"]}," will plead with me? for now, if I hold my tongue, I shall give up the ghost. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:19"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"20","sid":"JOB 13:20"},"Only do not two ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["things"]}," unto me: then will I not hide myself from thee. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:20"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"21","sid":"JOB 13:21"},"Withdraw thine hand far from me: and let not thy dread make me afraid. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:21"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"22","sid":"JOB 13:22"},"Then call thou, and I will answer: or let me speak, and answer thou me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:22"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"23","sid":"JOB 13:23"},"How many ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," mine iniquities and sins? make me to know my transgression and my sin. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:23"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"24","sid":"JOB 13:24"},"Wherefore hidest thou thy face, and holdest me for thine enemy? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:24"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"25","sid":"JOB 13:25"},"Wilt thou break a leaf driven to and fro? and wilt thou pursue the dry stubble? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:25"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"26","sid":"JOB 13:26"},"For thou writest bitter things against me, and makest me to possess the iniquities of my youth. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:26"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"27","sid":"JOB 13:27"},"Thou puttest my feet also in the stocks, and lookest narrowly unto all my paths; thou settest a print upon the heels of my feet. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:27"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"28","sid":"JOB 13:28"},"And he, as a rotten thing, consumeth, as a garment that is moth eaten. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 13:28"}]}]}
